TITLE      -Cross-section measurement for the threshold reactions 20377  1    6 
           Fe56(N,P)Mn56,Co59(N,a)Mn56 and Cu63(N,2N)Cu62 between 20377  1    7 
           12.6 and 19.6 MeV neutron energy -.                    20377  1    8 
FACILITY   (VDG)      3MeV van de graaff                          20377  1    9 
INC-SOURCE (D-T)   T(d,N)He4-reaction at 1 and 3 MeV deuteron     20377  1   10 
            energy using various emission angles                  20377  1   11 
SAMPLE     .Metallic                                              20377  1   12 
           .Discs 20 mm diameter, 5 mm thickness                  20377  1   13 
METHOD     (ACTIV)    Activation                                  20377  1   14 
DETECTOR   (NAICR)    Sodium-iodide crystal                       20377  1   15 
           for activity comparison with standard sources          20377  1   16 
           (TELES)    Recoil telescope                            20377  1   17 
           for neutron flux determination                         20377  1   18 
MONITOR    (1-H-1(N,EL)1-H-1,,SIG) Absolute measurement of the    20377  1   19 
            neutron flux was preformed with a proton recoil       20377  1   20 
            telescope of the Los Alamos type. The semi-empirical  20377  1   21 
            formula of gammel in fast neutron physics was used    20377  1   22 
            for the total N-P scattering cross section.           20377  1   23 
           .The relative excitation functions were normalised     20377  1   24 
            at 14.05 MeV for Co-59 and Cu-63, and at 14.80 MeV    20377  1   25 
            for Fe-56. The reproducibility of the absoute         20377  1   26 
            measurements was better than 0.7 percent.             20377  1   27 
STATUS     .Table 1, JNE/AB,19,73.                                20377  1   28 
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-1) Absolute neutron flux uncertainty, 4.0pc.      20377  1   29 
           (ERR-2) D-t neutron angular distribution uncertainty,  20377  1   30 
            value 2.5 percent.                                    20377  1   31 
           (ERR-3) Uncertainty from irradiation geometry, and     20377  1   32 
            absolute efficiency of the activity counters including20377  1   33 
            gamma ray absorption varies from 2.1 to 4.2 percent,  20377  1   34 
            a mean value of 3.0 percent is taken.                 20377  1   35 
           (ERR-4) Uncertainties from neutron absorption and      20377  1   36 
            scattering in the sample, chemical purity, and sample 20377  1   37 
            weight add quadratically to 0.6 percent.              20377  1   38 
           (ERR-T) Total uncertainty, quadratic addition of all   20377  1   39 
            contributions including statistical counting errors.  20377  1   40 
